{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"DOI:\"10.1038/s44318-025-00611-0\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"41162752","source":"MED","pmid":"41162752","pmcid":"PMC12669672","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC12669672"]},"doi":"10.1038/s44318-025-00611-0","title":"Structural insights into selective and dual antagonism of EP2 and EP4 prostaglandin receptors.","authorString":"Wu Y, Zhang H, Xu J, Wu K, Hu W, He X, Wang G, Wu C, Xu HE.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Wu Y","firstName":"Yanli","lastName":"Wu","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-4562-7397"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China. wuyanli@simm.ac.cn."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang H","firstName":"Heng","lastName":"Zhang","initials":"H","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9441-8277"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Xu J","firstName":"Jiuyin","lastName":"Xu","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-9411-955X"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Center for Medicinal Structural Biology, National Research Center for Translational Medicine at Shanghai, State Key Laboratory of Medical Genomics, Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, 200025, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wu K","firstName":"Kai","lastName":"Wu","initials":"K","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Hu W","firstName":"Wen","lastName":"Hu","initials":"W","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"He X","firstName":"Xinheng","lastName":"He","initials":"X","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang G","firstName":"Gaoming","lastName":"Wang","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Biliary-Pancreatic Surgery, Renji Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, 200025, Shanghai, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wu C","firstName":"Canrong","lastName":"Wu","initials":"C","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2272-3838"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Research Center for Medicinal Structural Biology, National Research Center for Translational Medicine at Shanghai, State Key Laboratory of Medical Genomics, Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, 200025, Shanghai, China. wcr13215@rjh.com.cn."}]}},{"fullName":"Xu HE","firstName":"H Eric","lastName":"Xu","initials":"HE","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6829-8144"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China. eric.xu@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"Research Center for Medicinal Structural Biology, National Research Center for Translational Medicine at Shanghai, State Key Laboratory of Medical Genomics, Ruijin Hospital, Shanghai Jiao Tong University School of Medicine, 200025, Shanghai, China. eric.xu@simm.ac.cn."},{"affiliation":"University of Chinese Academy of Sciences, Beijing, 100049, China. eric.xu@simm.ac.cn."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2272-3838"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6829-8144"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9441-8277"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0001-9411-955X"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-4562-7397"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","supporting_data","related_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"23","volume":"44","journalIssueId":4060146,"dateOfPublication":"2025 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2025,"printPublicationDate":"2025-12-01","journal":{"title":"The EMBO journal","medlineAbbreviation":"EMBO J","isoabbreviation":"EMBO J","issn":"0261-4189","nlmid":"8208664","essn":"1460-2075"}},"pubYear":"2025","pageInfo":"7242-7262","abstractText":"Prostaglandin E2 (PGE2) signaling through EP2 and EP4 receptors is crucial in regulating inflammation, pain, and cancer progression. While selective and dual antagonists for these receptors hold therapeutic potential, their binding mechanisms and selectivity have remained unclear. In this study, we present cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) structures of human EP2 and EP4 receptors in complex with selective antagonists PF-04418948 and grapiprant, as well as with the dual antagonist TG6-129. These structures reveal distinct binding pockets and interaction networks that dictate antagonist selectivity and efficacy. Notably, TG6-129 displays a novel binding mode, engaging deeply with EP2 while interacting more superficially with EP4 in a two-warhead manner. Furthermore, comparisons of active and inactive receptor structures elucidate the mechanisms underlying EP2 activation and antagonism. Overall, these findings provide a structural framework for understanding prostanoid receptor pharmacology and offer valuable insights for the rational design of improved selective and dual antagonists targeting EP2 and EP4 receptors.","affiliation":"State Key Laboratory of Drug Research, Shanghai Institute of Materia Medica, Chinese Academy of Sciences, 201203, Shanghai, China. wuyanli@simm.ac.cn.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"grantId":"XDB37030103","agency":"Chinese Academy of Science Strategic Priority Research Program","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"32130022","agency":"The National Natural Science Foundation of China","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"2022YFC2703105","agency":"The National Key Research and Development Program of China","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"82121005","agency":"The National Natural Science Foundation of China","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"2019SHZDZX02","agency":"Shanghai Municipal Science and Technology Major Project","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"2023707","agency":"Shanghai Post-doctoral Excellence Program","orderIn":0},{"grantId":"32301016","agency":"The National Natural Science Foundation of China","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cryoelectron Microscopy"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Binding Sites"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Protein Binding"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Models, Molecular"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Receptors, Prostaglandin E, EP2 Subtype","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AI","qualifierName":"antagonists & inhibitors","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Receptors, Prostaglandin E, EP4 Subtype","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"abbreviation":"AI","qualifierName":"antagonists & inhibitors","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism","majorTopic_YN":"N"},{"abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry","majorTopic_YN":"N"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["Ep4","Selective An